  "prefLabel": "En 1008.09 Final Utility Review and Metering",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1008.09 Final Utility Review and Metering. If the utility determines that a review of the facility or changes to the applicant’s meter are necessary, the following shall occur:\n\n(a) The utility shall review the facility or change the applicant’s meter within 10 business days of receiving the complete facility as-built documentation from the applicant;\n\n(b) If the facility passes the review, the utility shall provide written notice of such outcome to the applicant within 3 business days;\n\n(c) If the facility initially fails a utility review, the utility shall offer to conduct the inspection again at the applicant’s expense at a time mutually agreeable to both the utility and the applicant;\n\n(d) If the utility determines that the facility fails the review described in (c) above in this section, including the discovery of unapproved changes to the facility, the utility shall provide the applicant with a written explanation detailing the reasons for the failure and any standards violated within 3 business days; and\n\n(e) If the utility determines no review or changes to the applicant’s meter are necessary based on its review described in (a) above in this section, it shall notify the applicant within 3 business days of receiving the notice of the completion of construction.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
